---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LineChart from "../components/LineChart.astro";
import PeriodTable from "../components/PeriodTable.astro";
import { series, latest } from "../lib/data.js";
import { num, period } from "../lib/format.js";
import { config } from "../lib/config.js";
const repo = latest(series("repo_rate"));
const credit = latest(series("scb_credit_growth"));
---
<Base current="money" title="Money & banking">
  <h1>Money &amp; banking</h1>
  <p class="lede">What is RBI's policy stance, where are money-market rates, and how fast are bank credit and deposits growing? The policy repo rate is {num(repo.value, 2)}% ({period(repo.period, "D")}); bank credit grew {num(credit.value, 1)}% on a year earlier in the fortnight to {period(credit.period, "D")}.</p>
  <p class="chart-sub"><strong>New:</strong> <a href="/money/mpc-speak/">MPC Speak</a>, a hawk–dove reading of each MPC member's statement in the minutes.</p>

  <LineChart title="Policy corridor and the call rate" subtitle="Per cent; the call rate (WACR) normally trades between the SDF floor and the MSF ceiling"
    lines={[{ id: "msf_rate", label: "MSF (ceiling)", step: true }, { id: "repo_rate", label: "Repo", step: true }, { id: "sdf_rate", label: "SDF (floor)", step: true }, { id: "wacr", label: "Call rate (WACR)" }]} years={1} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Week-ended values from RBI's Weekly Statistical Supplement, plus daily readings of RBI's home page since 28 Oct 2026.</p>

  <h2>Bank credit and deposits</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Bank credit and deposit growth, as published" subtitle="Scheduled commercial banks, % change on a year earlier"
      lines={[{ id: "scb_credit_growth", label: "Credit" }, { id: "scb_deposits_growth", label: "Deposits" }]} years={1} />
    <LineChart title="Outstanding" subtitle="₹ lakh crore, scheduled commercial banks"
      lines={[{ id: "scb_deposits", label: "Deposits" }, { id: "scb_credit", label: "Credit" }]} years={1} />
  </div>
  <p class="chart-sub">RBI notes that these data include the effect of a non-bank merging into a bank, which lifts year-on-year growth; see the note in the WSS table.</p>

  <h2>Rates, recent weeks</h2>
  <PeriodTable heading="Per cent, week ended" n={6} digits={2} rows={[
    { id: "repo_rate" }, { id: "sdf_rate", indent: true }, { id: "msf_rate", indent: true },
    { id: "crr" }, { id: "slr" }, { id: "wacr" },
    { id: "tbill_91d_weekly" }, { id: "tbill_182d_weekly" }, { id: "tbill_364d_weekly" }, { id: "gsec_10y_par_fbil" },
  ]} freq="D" />

  <h2>MPC Speak</h2>
  <LineChart title="How hawkish is the MPC?" subtitle="Average tone of the six members' statements in the minutes; above zero leans hawkish, below zero dovish"
    lines={[{ id: "mpc_committee_tone", label: "Committee average" }]} reference={{ target: 0 }} years={11} />
  <p class="chart-sub">An original measure on {config.site.name}: phrase counts in each member's statement in the RBI minutes. <a href="/money/mpc-speak/">Member by member, and how the score works →</a></p>

  <h2>Still to come on this page</h2>
  <p class="chart-sub">LAF liquidity, sectoral credit, money supply (M3), a table of MPC decisions and vote splits. Checklist: docs/guidebook/05-pages/money-banking.md.</p>
</Base>
